  "notes": [
   "The catalog says 'Select a minimum of 18 total units combined from Group A & Group B', so Group A (Physical Sciences) and Group B (Biological Sciences) are recorded as one choose_units block with minimum 18. The courses keep catalog order: Group A first (ASTR through PHYS A285), then Group B (BIOL A100 through MRSC A288).",
   "Honors and 'or' alternatives print no units beside them in the catalog, so their units are null.",
   "GEOL A185H is printed as its own row, not as an 'or' option of GEOL A185, so it is recorded as a separate course. A reviewer should check whether it is meant as an honors alternative.",
   "The closed list stores PHYSA185 and PHYSA280 without a space. These were matched to catalog PHYS A185 and PHYS A280 and are not treated as catalog additions.",
   "PHYS A185H (honors alternative) is not in the closed list and is marked as a catalog addition.",
   "The degree total of 60 and OCC AS General Education of 21 are recorded as printed. A footnote says the Cal-GETC pattern (up to 34 units) may be substituted.",
   "Transferable electives are printed with 'varies' as needed to satisfy unit requirements, so electives_fill_degree is true.",
   "The single printed Program Learning Outcome is under the program overview and is recorded for this A.S. degree.",
   "The Program Sequence tab text is cut off at 'ELECTIV'. It holds no requirement data beyond the requirements tab."
